Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:11:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 073/154] feat(routing): route a matching url into its rule's
 space
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ONE throttle, where the feature used to have three hooks. A chrome::Navigate
hook, a window.open hook and a renderer-initiated link hook existed because
Swift needed three entry points, not because the problem has three cases: all
three are navigations, and a throttle sees every browser-mediated one. The peek
throttle already proved that layer works for a same-tab link click.

Its gates are deliberately looser than the peek throttle's. No user gesture, no
renderer initiator, no PAGE_TRANSITION_LINK - a typed URL carries none of those
and is the case routing exists for. Copying those gates would have skipped it
silently, which is why the scenario pins the typed case first.

The open lives on BrowserController, not in the throttle: it needs browser_,
which nothing outside that class can reach, and the same-profile and
cross-profile cases differ only in which controller answers - a split the
throttle has no business knowing. Same profile switches space and opens in
place. A different profile cannot, because a WebContents is bound to its
creating BrowserContext, so it reopens through that profile's controller.

Never opened synchronously from inside the throttle callback - that re-enters
the navigation machinery - so it posts the reopen and cancels silently, leaving
no error page. The reopen runs under the bypass, or two rules pointing at each
other's spaces would bounce one tab forever.

A rule naming a space that no longer exists routes nothing. Every miss and every
failed lookup PROCEEDs: routing is an enhancement, and a url it cannot place
must still open where it was going.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc | 2 ++
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn                      | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 71154cffec88c..0e4a11ed39e17 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -182,6 +182,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/translate/translate_service.h"
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_peek_navigation_throttle.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_routing_navigation_throttle.h"
 #endif
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/blocked_content/blocked_window_params.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/blocked_content/chrome_popup_navigation_delegate.h"
@@ -5671,6 +5672,7 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateThrottlesForNavigation(
   // Auto-peek. An off-site link click from a pinned or favourited
   // tab opens the Keyhole instead of navigating that tab away.
   atrium::AtriumPeekNavigationThrottle::MaybeCreateAndAdd(registry);
+  atrium::AtriumRoutingNavigationThrottle::MaybeCreateAndAdd(registry);
 #endif
 }
 
